"# Jordimp & Co. — full reference

Jordi Marçal Poy — Senior Backend Engineer (Java · Python · AI/LLM).
One-person engineering firm, est. 2017, Barcelona. Languages: English, Español, Català.
Contact: jordi.marsal@gmail.com · https://github.com/jordimarsal · https://www.linkedin.com/in/jordi-marsal-poy

## The building

## F3 — Research & Retrieval

The top floor ships AI like infrastructure: deterministic cores, golden Q/A sets, evals gated in CI. If a model can’t be measured, it doesn’t ship.

Projects:
  - CodebaseRAG (2026): Hexagonal RAG over your own codebase, with a deterministic, eval-first core: ingest, query, and CI-gated retrieval evals. Stack: Python 3.13, FastAPI, pgvector, Qdrant, Ollama, Langfuse, mypy strict. https://github.com/jordimarsal/codebaserag
  - Interview Simulator (2026): Voice interview simulator: a local LLM plays the interviewer and Whisper handles transcription, so you can rehearse technical interviews fully offline. Stack: Whisper, Local LLM. https://github.com/jordimarsal/interview-simulator
  - Bible Text Analysis (2019): NLP study on the Bible: web scraping, NLTK processing, LDA topic modeling and sentiment analysis — my Data Science roots. Stack: Python, NLTK, LDA, Jupyter. https://github.com/jordimarsal/bible_text_analysis

## F2 — Transport & Telemetry

Event pipelines, rate limits and health tracking with honest failure modes. When a dependency goes down, callers know exactly where they stand.

Projects:
  - Kafka Adapter Telemetry (2026): Event-driven adapter telemetry: a Kafka gateway + hub pipeline with idempotent Oracle persistence, per-adapter health tracking, alerting, and a live SSE mission-control dashboard. Stack: Java 25, Spring Boot 4.1, Kafka, Oracle, Flyway, Testcontainers, SSE. https://github.com/jordimarsal/kafka-adapter-telemetry
  - Redis Toolkit (2026): Rate-limiting toolkit for LLM gateways: atomic token-bucket quotas, pluggable stores, honest failure modes — with a Javalin gateway demo exposing an OpenAI-style endpoint. Stack: Java, Javalin, Redis, Testcontainers. https://github.com/jordimarsal/redis-toolkit
  - Product Offers API (2023 - 2026): Technical assessment: a product offers REST API — price inquiries by date, product and brand, served with Spring Boot. Stack: Java 17, Spring Boot 3.2, H2, JUnit 5, Mockito. https://github.com/jordimarsal/product-offers

## F1 — Tooling & Platform

The workshop floor: a multi-agent SDD harness, CLIs that do one thing well, and tooling kept intentionally small. Everything it needs, nothing it doesn’t.

Projects:
  - Harness Standard (2026): A standardized multi-agent harness for Claude Code and OpenCode: Spec-Driven Development roles (Leader, Spec Author, Implementer, Reviewer) installed into any project with a single command. Stack: Agents, SDD, CLI, Conventions. https://github.com/jordimarsal/harness-standard
  - Rustcut (2024 - 2026): Tiny URL shortener in Rust: a deliberately minimalist REST API on Actix-web with SQLite storage. Stack: Rust, Actix-web, SQLite. https://github.com/jordimarsal/rustcut
  - MD Mermaid PDF (2025 - 2026): CLI that renders Markdown with Mermaid diagrams straight to PDF, engineered with TDD, mypy strict and CI. Stack: Python, Markdown, Mermaid, GitHub Actions. https://github.com/jordimarsal/md-mermaid-pdf
  - MCP Transparent PNG (2026): MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that makes PNG colors transparent (alpha channel) with rgb/auto/greenscreen modes. Stack: Python 3.13, MCP, Pillow, GitHub Actions. https://github.com/jordimarsal/mcp-transparent-png
  - Spring Boot Casino (2020 - 2026): Technical assessment: a casino betting domain modeled in Spring Boot following a hexagonal architecture. Stack: Java, Spring Boot, Hexagonal Architecture. https://github.com/jordimarsal/spring-boot-casino

## M — People & Principles

The mezzanine keeps the house rules: SOLID, Clean Code and TDD as daily practice, I/O at the edges, and knowledge that flows across the team.


## F0 — Operations

The ground floor keeps the record: every engagement since 2017, what shipped, and what it was built with. One ledger, four chapters, zero rewrites.


## B — Front Desk

The door is always open. Questions about a floor, a repo, or a hire? Walk straight in — no appointment, no gatekeeper, no tracking scripts.


